WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.840
In 1977, the world recorded its
last natural case of smallpox.

2
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:09.420
In 1980, it was declared eradicated.

3
00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:14.310
A disease that killed about 30
per cent of its cases was gone.

4
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.320
Malaria is still with us.

5
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:20.000
So is flu, which caused pandemics in 1957,

6
00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:23.150
1968 and 2009.

7
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.230
So why could smallpox be beaten, while
malaria and flu are still with us?

8
00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:32.330
In this mission, you'll learn the
terms for how far a disease spreads,

9
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.670
from endemic to pandemic.

10
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.620
Then you'll compare five
diseases, from cholera to malaria,

11
00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.360
one card at a time.

12
00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:44.040
Your mission: find out what
makes a disease hard to beat.
